    "Do_Immediate_Amplitude": {
      "scpi": ":IMMediate:AMPLitude",
      "scpiFast": ":IMM:AMPL",
      "description": "This command directly programs the immediate current level of the power module",
      "subsystem": "IMM",
      "unverified": true,
      "retired": true,
      "retired_because": "HP 66lxxA MPS Programming Guide 5959-3362 (https://xdevs.com/doc/HP_Agilent_Keysight/661xxA_programming.pdf) pp. 35, 48: the manual writes [SOURce]:CURRent[:LEVel] [:IMMediate][:AMPLitude] and [SOURce]:VOLTage[:LEVel] [:IMMediate][:AMPlitude] with a space before [:IMMediate]; the scraper split there, so `:IMMediate:AMPlitude` alone is a fragment with no root — the real commands are CURR/VOLT (SOUR:CURR:LEV:IMM:AMPL, SOUR:VOLT:LEV:IMM:AMPL)"
    },
