    "Get_Values": {
      "scpi": "MEAS:VOLT?;:MEAS:CURR?",
      "description": "Measured output voltage and current.",
      "group": "Readback Queries",
      "subsystem": "MEASure",
      "returns": {
        "count": 2,
        "separator": ";",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "voltage",
            "type": "NR3",
            "unit": "V"
          },
          {
            "name": "current",
            "type": "NR3",
            "unit": "A"
          }
        ]
      },
      "notes": "Was `INST:NSEL <chan>;MEAS:VOLT?;MEAS:CURR?` — see the module docstring; it answered nothing here on either count. Verified on the 66101A at gpib7,30,0, 2026-08-08."
    },
    "Read_Values": {
      "scpi": "MEAS:VOLT?;:MEAS:CURR?",
      "description": "Read Voltage and Current",
      "returns": {
        "count": 2,
        "separator": ";",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "voltage",
            "type": "NR3",
            "unit": "V"
          },
          {
            "name": "current",
            "type": "NR3",
            "unit": "A"
          }
        ]
      },
      "group": "MPS Metering",
      "notes": "Undefined on a module addressed at its own GPIB secondary address, which is how all seven on this bench are wired — `SYST:ERR?` answers -113 after it, and it silently kills any reply chained behind it. Correct only for a mainframe addressed as one instrument. Checked 2026-08-08. Was `INST:NSEL <chan>;MEAS:VOLT?;MEAS:CURR?`: the 661xxA has no INSTrument subsystem (the HP 661xxA MPS Programming Guide 5959-3362 has none) — each module is its own GPIB secondary address (Dev730-N), and the bench answered -113 after `INST:NSEL`, which also killed every reply chained behind it. The module's own commands, each from the root (p. 41, 48, 35, 33).",
      "unverified": true,
      "alias_of": "Get_Values"
    },
