          {
            "name": "oper_condition",
            "type": "NR1"
          }
        ]
      },
      "notes": "The panel's whole readback: every control on the module page names this as its `readback`, so ONE query after any write leaves nothing on screen that the instrument has not just confirmed.\n\noper_condition is the Operation Condition register. Bit 8 (256) is CV and bit 10 (1024) is CC — measured, not assumed: output on at 2 V into no load reads +256, and the same 2 V behind a 1 mA limit reads +1024 with MEAS:VOLT? collapsed to 0. Output off reads +0.\n\n`:STAT:QUES:COND?` is deliberately NOT chained on the end. It answers on its own and in a pair with :STAT:OPER:COND?, but appended to these six the whole reply is lost — and a chain that fails takes the five good values with it. Verified on the 66101A at gpib7,30,0, 2026-08-08."
    }
  }
}
